          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-operad
            is to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            is to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %p
            So, roughly, an
            = succeed "-operad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of operations that take these inputs to that output.
          %p
            There is a fairly evident notion of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebra+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} ∞-algebra over an (∞,1)-operad
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+algebra"}> E-∞ algebra
                s
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"}> L-∞ algebra
                s;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"}> A-∞ algebra
                s.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Operads form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Operad"} (∞,1)Operad
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Many equivalent models for
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The dendroidal model of
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Cisinski
                = succeed "\u2013" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Moerdijk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Weiss
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Lurie
            %li
              %p
                The complete Segal operad model of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"} Barwick
            %li
              %p
                The equifibered model of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Haugseng
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Kock
                and
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shaul+Barkan"} Barkan
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Steinebrunner"} Steinebrunner
            %li
              %p
                The analytic monad model of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} Gepner
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Haugseng
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Kock
            %li
              %p
                The “Symmetric sequences in a closed symmetric monoidal model category” model of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"} Berger
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Moerdijk
          %p
            We focus on the first two. The first one models
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            The second models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
            of an operad.
          %h3#in_terms_of_dendroidal_sets In terms of dendroidal sets
          %p
            Here
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            is formulated in terms of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            whose fibrant objects are the
            = succeed "s" do
              %strong quasi-operad
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
          %p
            So the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presention
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-operads." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
            enriched over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞ algebra
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+BV-algebra"} homotopy BV-algebra
            = succeed "-operads." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h3#InTermsOfInfinityCategoriesOfOperators
            In terms of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            encodes and is encoded by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_A
            = succeed "-operators" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of operators.
          %p
            In this approach an
            = succeed "-operad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes
            is regarded as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            – the unary part of the
            = succeed "-operad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo ×
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\times n} \to C
          %p
            This and the conditions on these are encoded in requiring that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes
            is an
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes \to \Gamma
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+Gamma-category"} Segal's category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            of pointed finite sets, satisfying some conditions.
          %p
            In particular, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            yields an example of an
            = succeed "-operad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em defined
            as
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes \to \Gamma
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration"} coCartesian fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            for more comments and references on higher operads in this context.)
          %p
            This is the approach described in (
            %a{:href => "#LurieCommutative"}> LurieCommutative
            )
          %h4#BasicDefinitions Basic definitions
          %p
            We are to generalize the following construction from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to FinSet^{*/}
              for its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are finite sequences (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"}> tuples
                  ) of objects of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒪
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1, \cdots, X_{n_1}) \to (Y_1, \cdots, Y_{n_2})
                  are given by a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon \langle n_1\rangle \to \langle n_2\rangle
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
                  together with a collection of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multimorphisms"} multimorphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                  %mo {
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mi i
                                  %mo }
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msup
                                    %mi α
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo {
                                    %mi j
                                    %mo }
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mi j
                              %mo )
                            %mo }
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi j
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left\{
                        \\phi_j \in \mathcal{O}\left( \left\{ X_i\right\}_{i \in \alpha^{-1}\left\{j\right\}} , Y_j \right)
                        \\right\}_{1 \leq j \leq n_2}
                        \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to FinSet^{*/}
              is the evident
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ) this is construction 2.1.1.7.
          %p
            This motivates the following definition of the generalization of this situation to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
          #FinSetPointed.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
              for the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+Gamma-category"}> Segal's Gamma-category
              ).
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle n\rangle
                    \\coloneqq
                    {*} \coprod [n]
                    \\in
                    FinSet^{*/}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed set
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              elements.
            %p
              A morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  is called an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inert+morphism"} inert morphism
                  if it is a surjection, and an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                  on those elements that are not sent to the base point. That is, the preimage of every non-base point is a singleton.
              %li
                %p
                  called an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/active+morphism"} active morphism
                  if only the basepoint goes to the basepoint.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq n
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho^i \colon \langle n\rangle \to \langle 1\rangle
            %p
              for the inert morphism that sends all but the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %p
              Notice that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is a unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/active+morphism"} active morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle n\rangle \to \langle 1\rangle
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 2.1.1.8
            )
          #InfinityOperadByCategoryOfOperators.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                \-category of operators of an
                = succeed "-operad" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              is a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p \colon \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to FinSet^{*/}
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              such that the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inert+morphism"} inert morphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
                  and every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  over it, there is a lift to a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+morphism"} coCartesian morphism
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mo ⊗
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \langle n_1\rangle \to \langle n_2\rangle
                  inert, there is an induced
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f_!
                        \\colon
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle n_1\rangle}
                        \\to
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle n_2\rangle}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  The coCartesian lifts of the inert projection morphisms induce an equivalence of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{\otimes}
                  between maps into multiple objects and the products of the maps into the separete objects:
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \langle n_1 \rangle \to \langle n_2 \rangle
                  write
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi f
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes_f(-,-) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{O}^\otimes(-,-)
                  for the components of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
                  covering
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  = succeed "-functor" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi f
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi k
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi ρ
                              %mi i
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_f(C_1,C_2)
                        \\to
                        \\underset{1 \leq k \leq n_2}{\prod}
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\rho^i\circ f}(C_1,(C_2)_i)
                %p
                  induced as above is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+infinity-groupoids"} equivalence
              %li
                %p
                  For every finite collection of objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1, \cdots c_n \in \mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle 1\rangle}
                  there exists a multiobject
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∈
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in \mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle n\rangle}
                  and a collection of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+morphisms"} coCartesian morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C \to C_i\}
                  covering
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ρ
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^i
                %p
                  Equivalently (given the first two conditions): for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  the
                  = succeed "-functors" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo !
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(\rho^i)_!\}_{1 \leq i \leq n}
                  induce an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ×
                              %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle n\rangle}
                        \\to
                        (\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle 1\rangle})^{\times^n}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 2.1.1.10, remark 2.1.1.14
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The conditions in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityOperadByCategoryOfOperators"}
              mean that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to FinSet^{*/}
              encodes
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ≔
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                            %mo ⊗
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} \coloneqq \mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle 1\rangle}
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  an
                  = succeed "-ary" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  = succeed "-functor" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo ×
                            %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo =
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{O}^{n}
                        \=
                        (\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle 1\rangle})^{\times n}
                        \\simeq
                        \\mathcal{O}^{\otimes}_{\langle n\rangle}
                        \\to
                        \\mathcal{O}^\otimes_{\langle 1\rangle}
                        \=
                        \\mathcal{O}
                %p
                  induced by the unique
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/active+morphism"} active morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle n\rangle \to \langle 1\rangle
              %li
                %p a coherently associative multicomposition of these operations.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The notion of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityOperadByCategoryOfOperators"}
              may also be called a
              %strong
                symmetric
                = succeed "-multicategory" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  colored
                  = succeed "-operad" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %em colors
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
          %p
            We now turn to the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of
            = succeed "-operads." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          #InertMorphismsInInfinityOperad.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given an
              = succeed "-operad" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to FinSet^{*/}
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityOperadByCategoryOfOperators"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes
              is called an
              %strong inert morphism
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(f)
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inert+morphism"} inert morphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
                  by def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FinSetPointed"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+morphism"} coCartesian morphism
          #MorphismOfInfinityOperads.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} morphism of (∞,1)-operads
              is a map between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+operators"} (∞,1)-categories of operators
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
              that preserves the inert morphisms of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InertMorphismsInInfinityOperad"}
          %p
            Morphisms of operads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_1 \to \to \mathcal{O}_2
            can be understood equivalently as exhibiting an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_2
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_1, \mathcal{O}_2
              to
              = succeed "-operads," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi qCat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msup
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alg_{\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{O}_2)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    qCat_{/FinSet^{*/}}(\mathcal{O}_1, \mathcal{O}_2)
            %p
              for the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-functor (∞,1)-category
              on those that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} morphisms of (∞,1)-operads
              by def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MorphismOfInfinityOperads"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 2.1.2.7
            ).
          %p We also have the notion of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} fibration of (∞,1)-operads
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} coCartesian fibration of (∞,1)-operads
                \.
          %p See there for more details.
          %h4#ModelForinfOpera
            Model for
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi Oper
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat_{Oper}
            of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p There exists a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} Op_{(\infty,1)}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  whose underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  has
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"}> object
                      s are
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                      equipped with a morphism
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                            %mo →
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to N(FinSet_*)
                      such that marked edges map to inert morphisms in
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
                      (those for which the preimage of the marked point contains just the marked point)
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> morphism
                      s are morphisms of
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to T
                      such that the triangle
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi S
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo →
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi T
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo ↘
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo ↙
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi N
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi FinSet
                                      %mo *
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            \\array{
                            S &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; T
                            \\\
                            \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                            \\\
                            \&amp;&amp; N(FinSet_*)
                            }
                    %p commutes;
              %li
                %p
                  which is canonically an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              %li
                %p
                  and whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model structure
                  is given by
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      cofibrations are those morphisms whose underlying morphisms of
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  %li
                    %p
                      weak equivalences are those morphisms
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to T
                      such that for all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo →
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to N(FinSet_*)
                      that are
                      = succeed "-categories" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn ∞
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+object"} hom object
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒫
                            %msub
                              %mi Op
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi 𝒫
                            %msub
                              %mi Op
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            \\mathcal{P}Op_\infty(T,A) \to
                            \\mathcal{P}Op_\infty(S,A)
                    %p is a homotopy equivalence of simplicial sets.
                  %li
                    %p
                      an object is fibrant if and only if it is an
                      = succeed "-category" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn ∞
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p This is prop 1.8 4 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em Commutative algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/DAG-III.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            We list some examples of
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+operators"} (∞,1)-categories of operators
            by def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityOperadByCategoryOfOperators"}
          %p
            The first basic examples to follow are in fact all given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} of operators
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              functor on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{*/}
              exhibits an
              = succeed "-operad." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mn .1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty.1)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+operad"} commutative operad
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Comm
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi id
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Comm^\otimes = FinSet^{*/} \stackrel{id}{\to} FinSet^{*/}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebras+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-algebras over an (∞,1)-operad
              over this
              = succeed "-operad" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} E-∞ algebras
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+operad"} associative operad
              has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Assoc
                      %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Assoc^\otimes
              the category whose objects are the natural numbers, whose
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+orders"} total orders
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements, equivalently the elements of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebras+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-algebras over an (∞,1)-operad
              over this
              = succeed "-operad" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} A-∞ algebras
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ) this is remark 4.1.1.4.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad+for+modules+over+an+algebra"} operad for modules over an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LM
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+operad"} colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are two elements, to be denoted
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔫
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{n}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multimorphisms"} multimorphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i)_{i = 1}^n \to Y
                  form
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathfrak{a}
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i = \mathfrak{a}
                      for all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                      then: the set of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
                      on
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      elements, equivalently the elements of the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Σ
                                %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔫
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathfrak{n}
                      and exactly one of the
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔫
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i = \mathfrak{n}
                      then: the set of linear order
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo &lt;
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{i_1 \lt \cdots \lt i_n\}
                      such that
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔫
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i_n} = \mathfrak{n}
                  %li
                    %p otherwise: the empty set;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  is given by composition of linear orders as for the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+operad"} associative operad
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebras+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-algebras over an (∞,1)-operad
              over this
              = succeed "-operad" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} A-∞ algebras
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-modules"} (∞,1)-modules
              over them.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ) this appears as def. 4.2.1.1.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad+for+bimodules+over+algebras"} operad for bimodules over algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BMod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BMod
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+operad"} colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are three elements, to be denoted
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔞
                          %mo −
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔞
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}_-, \mathfrak{a}_+
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔫
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{n}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multimorphisms"} multimorphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i)_{i = 1}^n \to Y
                  form
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo −
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathfrak{a}_-
                      and all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo −
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i = \mathfrak{a}_-
                      then: the set of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
                      of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      elements;
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathfrak{a}_*
                      and all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i = \mathfrak{a}_*
                      then again: the set of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
                      of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      elements;
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      = succeed ":" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi Y
                              %mo =
                              %mi 𝔫
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathfrak{n}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo &lt;
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{i_1 \lt \cdots \lt i_n\}
                      such that there is exactly one index
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_k
                      with
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi k
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝔫
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i_k} = \mathfrak{n}
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo −
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i_j} = \mathfrak{a}_-
                      for all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \lt k
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo +
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i_j} = \mathfrak{a}_+
                      for all
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi k
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \gt k
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  is given by the composition of linear orders as for the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+operad"} associative operad
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebras+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-algebras over an (∞,1)-operad
              over this
              = succeed "-operad" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} A-∞ algebras
              with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-bimodule"} (∞,1)-bimodule
              over them.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation Equivalence between the two definitions
          %p
            The dendroidal and category of operads models are equivalent, as shown in e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hinich22"} Hinich-Moerdijk
          %p
            There is an obvious way to regard a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
            as an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (dendroidal
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi N
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega : \Omega \hookrightarrow Op \stackrel{C_{(-)}}{\to}
                    Cat/FinSet_* \stackrel{N}{\to}
                    \\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
            %p be the dendroidal object given by the following composition:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \hookrightarrow Op
                  is the functor from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                  to the category of symmetric colored
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Op
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op \stackrel{C_{(-)}}{\to} Cat/FinSet_*
                  sends an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
                  to its
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi N
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %msub
                          %mi Op
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Cat/FinSet_*
                        \\stackrel{N}{\to} \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
                  takes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
                  of this category, regarded as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
                  over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi FinSet
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(FinSet_*)
          %p
            Following the general pattern of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (dendroidal nerve of Lurie-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-operad)
            %p The functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %msub
                          %mi Op
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_d :=
                    Hom_{\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}}(\omega(-), -):
                    \\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)} \to dSet
            %p
              that sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to N(FinSet_*)
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              to the set of morphisms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(T)
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %msub
                          %mi Op
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_d(A) : T \mapsto Hom_{\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}}(\omega(T), A)
            %p
              is the
              %strong dendroidal nerve
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .standout
            %p
              One expects that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              and indeed a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the above model category structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p The dendroidal nerve functor has the following properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  of a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi dSet
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ←
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %msub
                          %mi Op
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        C_{(-)} : dSet \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
                        \: N_d
              %li
                %p it sends fibrant objects to fibrant objects
                %p
                  i.e. it sends
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  = succeed "-operads" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %li
                %p
                  it sends objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : A \to N(FinSet_*)
                  that come from grouplike
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              %li
                %p
                  it sends objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : A \to N(FinSet_*)
                  that come from
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-categories
                  to dendroidal sets that have the extension property with respect to at least one outer horn
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi v
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{v} T
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in T
                  an
                  = succeed "-corolla," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  sends cofibrations to cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations with cofibrant domain to acyclic cofibrations.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %strong> respect for fibrant objects
              \. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to N(FinSet_*)
              is fibrant, then in particual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"} weak Kan complex
              hence has the extension property with respect to all inner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              inclusions of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
              has the extension property with respect to all inner horn inclusions of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
            %p
              By an (at the moment unpublished) result by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Moerdijk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
              with respect to inner horn inclusions of trees is equivalend to right lifting property with respect to inclusions of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
            %p
              For this the extension property means that if we find a collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C_{k_i} \to N_d(A)\} = Sp(T)
              of corollas in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
              that match at some inputs and output, then these can be composed to an image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to N_d(A)
              of the corresponding tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
            %p
              An image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
              is an image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(T)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(A)
              every tree may be represented as the composite of a sequence of morphisms each of which consists of precisely one of the corollas
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{k_i}
              in parallel to identity morphisms. This way gluing the tree from the corollas is a matter of composing a sequence of edges in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"} weak Kan complex
            %p
              %strong symmetric monoidal product and outer horn lifting
            %p
              As described at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Delta^1 \to A
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is coCartesian if for all diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mn 0
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Delta^{0,1}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^f
                    \\\
                    \\Lambda^n_0 &amp;\to &amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; N(FinSet_*)
                    }
            %p
              of 0-horn lifting problems where the first edge of the horn is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              itself, there exists a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mn 0
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Delta^{0,1}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^f
                    \\\
                    \\Lambda^n_0 &amp;\to &amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; N(FinSet_*)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              the parallel application of an
              = succeed "-corolla" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi v
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_v T \to N_d(A)
              for which the vertex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v : C_n \to N_d(A)
              maps to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
              has the extension property with respect to the inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi d
                      %mi T
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_d T \hookrightarrow T
            %p
              %strong the left adjoint and its respect for cofibrations
            %p
              By general nonsense the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_{(-)} : dSet \to \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi P
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_P = \int^{T \in \Omega} \omega(T) \cdot P(T)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where in the integrand we have the tautological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensoring
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega : \Omega \to \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
              is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
              for the ordinary category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              regarded as a simplicially enriched category by the canonical embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi SSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \hookrightarrow SSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv N_d
              is defined entirely in
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
              and hence is a simplicial adjunction.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
              has a set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generating cofibrations
              given by the boundary inclusions of trees.
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Omega[T] \hookrightarrow \Omega[T]
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : P \hookrightarrow Q
              an acyclic cofibration with cofibrant domain, we need to check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_f : C_X \to C_Y
              is a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %msub
                        %mi Op
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi Op
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}(C_Y,A) \to
                    \\mathcal{P}Op_{(\infty,1)}(C_X,A)
            %p
              is a weak equivalence in the standard
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv N_d
              this is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dSet(f,N_d(A))
                    \:
                    dSet(Y,N_d(A)) \to
                    dSet(X,N_d(A))
            %p
              being a weak equivalence. By the above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d(A)
              is fibrant. By section 8.4 of the lecture notes on dendroidal sets cited at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
              a morphism between cofibrant dendroidal sets is a weak equivalence precisely if homming it into any fibrant dendroidal set produces an equivalence of homotopy categories.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a weak equivalence between cofibrant objects by assumption, it follows that indeed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet(f,N_d(A))
              is a weak equivalence for all fibrant
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %blockquote
              %p (AHM, or does it? there is a prob here, but I need to run now…)
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_f
              is a weak equivalence.
