                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"}> generalized (∞,1)-operad
                    ,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} family of (∞,1)-operads
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"}> algebra over an (∞,1)-operad
                    ,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on algebras over an operad
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+an+algebra+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"}> module over an algebra over an (∞,1)-operad
                      ,
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+modules+over+an+algebra+over+an+operad"} model structure on modules over an algebra over an operad
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} coherent (∞,1)-operad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operadic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} operadic (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+of+operads"} cohomology of operads
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+pattern"} algebraic pattern
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The formulation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Ittay Weiss
                %em Dendroidal sets
                (
                %a{:href => "http://cat.inist.fr/?aModele=afficheN&cpsidt=20087314"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em Dendroidal sets as models for homotopy operads
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0902.1954"}> arXiv
                ) .
          %p Here are two blog entries on talks on this stuff:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/02/dendroidal_sets.html"} Dendroidal Sets and Infinity-Operads
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/02/moerdijk_on_infinityoperads.html"} Moerdijk on Infinity Operads
          %p
            The formulation in terms of an
            = succeed "-version" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+operators"} category of operators
            is introduced in
          %ul#LurieCommutative
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Commutative+Algebra"} Commutative Algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/DAG-III.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and further discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ek-Algebras"} Ek-Algebras
              \.
          %p Now in section 2 of the textbook
          %ul#Lurie
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            The equivalence between the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"}> Gijs Heuts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"} Vladimir Hinich
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em The equivalence between Lurie’s model and the dendroidal model for infinity-operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.3658"}> arXiv:1305.3658
              )
          %p and made symmetric monoidal in
          %ul
            %li#Hinich22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the equivalence of the Lurie’s ∞-operads and dendroidal ∞-operads
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.14033"} arXiv:2206.14033
          %p Further equivalence to Barwick’s complete Segal operads is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Hongyi Chu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"} Gijs Heuts
              %em
                Two models for the homotopy theory of
                = succeed "-operads" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03826"}> arXiv:1606.03826
              )
          %p
            For an account in terms of
            %em analytic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Joachim Kock
              = succeed "," do
                %em ∞-Operads as Analytic Monads
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06469"} arXiv:1712.06469
          %p
            For an account in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %em symmetric monoidal categories and equifibrations
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Joachim Kock
                = succeed "," do
                  %em ∞-operads as symmetric monoidal ∞-categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.12975"} arXiv:2106.12975
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shaul+Barkan"}> Shaul Barkan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Steinebrunner"} Jan Steinebrunner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The equifibered approach to ∞-properads
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.02576"} arXiv:2211.02576
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann-Hilton+argument"} Eckmann-Hilton argument
            for (∞,1)-operads:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomer+Schlank"}> Tomer Schlank
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lior+Yanovski"} Lior Yanovski
              = succeed "," do
                %em The ∞-Categorical Eckmann-Hilton Argument
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.06006"} arXiv:1808.06006
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2019.19.3119"} doi:10.2140/agt.2019.19.3119
